IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4, Division 7 -- Title and transfers, first half: nature of shares, numbering, certificates, duplicate seal, lost certificates (ss 121 to 125). Layer 1, part agent sgj.
-- Source file lines 10475-10602. The text is a rendering of the Act, not the official text.
-- HOW IT IS MODELLED: as in sgj-div5-debentures.l4 (decision functions answering MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING otherwise).

§ `Section 121: nature of shares`

-- The shares or other interest of any member is movable property, transferable in the manner the constitution provides, and not of the nature of immovable property.
-- src:10479 | 121. The shares or other interest of any member in a company is
-- src:10480 | movable property, transferable in the manner provided by the
-- src:10481 | constitution, and is not of the nature of immovable property.
@ref s 121 (src:10479-10481)
GIVEN `the thing is a share or other interest of a member in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 the share or other interest of a member is movable property` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a share or other interest of a member in a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The shares or other interest of any member in a company is movable property" -- the section speaks of a member's share or interest

@ref s 121 (src:10479-10481)
GIVEN `the thing is a share or other interest of a member in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 the share or other interest of a member is of the nature of immovable property` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a share or other interest of a member in a company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not of the nature of immovable property"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of a member's share or interest

@ref s 121 (src:10479-10481)
GIVEN `the thing is a share or other interest of a member in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is made in the manner provided by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 the share or other interest of a member is transferable in the manner provided by the constitution` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a share or other interest of a member in a company` AND `the transfer is made in the manner provided by the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "transferable in the manner provided by the constitution" -- a transfer in another manner is not covered

§ `Section 122: numbering of shares`

-- s 122(2)(a): fully paid up and equal ranking: none of those shares need have a distinguishing number, so long as each remains so.
-- src:10490 | (2) Despite subsection (1) —
-- src:10492 | (a) if at any time all the issued shares in a company or all the
-- src:10493 | issued shares therein of a particular class are fully paid up
-- src:10494 | and rank equally for all purposes, none of those shares need
-- src:10495 | thereafter have a distinguishing number so long as each of
-- src:10496 | those shares remains fully paid up and ranks equally for all
-- src:10497 | purposes with all shares of the same class for the time
-- src:10498 | being issued and fully paid up; or
@ref s 122(2)(a) (src:10490-10498)
GIVEN `all the issued shares in the company, or all the issued shares of a particular class, are fully paid up and rank equally for all purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each of those shares remains fully paid up and ranks equally for all purposes with all shares of the same class for the time being issued and fully paid up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(2)(a) the shares need no distinguishing number` MEANS
    IF `all the issued shares in the company, or all the issued shares of a particular class, are fully paid up and rank equally for all purposes` AND `each of those shares remains fully paid up and ranks equally for all purposes with all shares of the same class for the time being issued and fully paid up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite subsection (1) — (a) if ... none of those shares need ... have a distinguishing number so long as ..." -- an exception that applies only on its conditions; outside it the exception is silent

-- s 122(2)(b): all issued shares evidenced by certificates under s 123, each certificate numbered, the number recorded in the register of members.
-- src:10500 | (b) if all the issued shares in a company are evidenced by
-- src:10501 | certificates in accordance with section 123 and each
-- src:10502 | certificate is distinguished by an appropriate number and
-- src:10503 | that number is recorded in the register of members, none of
-- src:10504 | those shares need have a distinguishing number.
@ref s 122(2)(b) (src:10500-10504)
GIVEN `all the issued shares in the company are evidenced by certificates in accordance with section 123` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each certificate is distinguished by an appropriate number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that number is recorded in the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(2)(b) the shares need no distinguishing number` MEANS
    IF `all the issued shares in the company are evidenced by certificates in accordance with section 123` AND `each certificate is distinguished by an appropriate number` AND `that number is recorded in the register of members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or (b) if all the issued shares ... none of those shares need have a distinguishing number" -- an exception that applies only on its conditions

-- s 122(1): each share must be distinguished by an appropriate number, despite (2) the shares of (2)(a) or (b) need not be.
-- src:10487 | 122.—(1) Each share in a company must be distinguished by an
-- src:10488 | appropriate number.
@ref s 122(1) (src:10487-10488)
GIVEN `limb (a) of subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) of subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(1) the share must be distinguished by an appropriate number` MEANS
    IF `limb (a) of subsection (2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `limb (b) of subsection (2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite subsection (1) — ... none of those shares need ... have a distinguishing number"
    ELSE JUST TRUE    -- "Each share in a company must be distinguished by an appropriate number" -- a duty

§ `Section 123: certificate to be evidence of title`

DECLARE `s 123 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 123(2) issue the share certificate under the seal and stating what the subsection requires`

-- src:10508 | 123.—(1) A certificate under the common or official seal of a
-- src:10509 | company specifying any shares held by any member of the company
-- src:10510 | is prima facie evidence of the title of the member to the shares.
@ref s 123(1) (src:10508-10510)
GIVEN `the certificate is under the common or official seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate specifies shares held by a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(1) the certificate is prima facie evidence of the title of the member to the shares` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is under the common or official seal of the company` AND `the certificate specifies shares held by a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate under the common or official seal of a company specifying any shares held by any member ... is prima facie evidence" -- without the seal or the specification the subsection is silent

-- s 123(2): the seal (common, or official for shares on a branch register) and the three things the certificate states.
-- src:10512 | (2) Every share certificate must be under the common seal of the
-- src:10513 | company or, in the case of a share certificate relating to shares on a
-- src:10514 | branch register, the official seal of the company and must state as at
-- src:10515 | the date of the issue of the certificate —
-- src:10517 | (a) the name of the company and the authority under which the
-- src:10518 | company is constituted;
-- src:10523 | (b) the address of the registered office of the company in
-- src:10524 | Singapore, or, where the certificate is issued by a branch
-- src:10525 | office, the address of that branch office; and
-- src:10527 | (c) the class of the shares, whether the shares are fully or partly
-- src:10528 | paid up and the amount (if any) unpaid on the shares.
@ref s 123(2) (src:10512-10528)
GIVEN `the certificate relates to shares on a branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is under the common seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is under the official seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the name of the company and the authority under which the company is constituted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the address of the registered office of the company in Singapore or, where it is issued by a branch office, the address of that branch office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the class of the shares, whether they are fully or partly paid up and the amount (if any) unpaid on them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(2) the share certificate is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    (IF `the certificate relates to shares on a branch register` THEN `the certificate is under the official seal of the company` ELSE `the certificate is under the common seal of the company`)
      AND `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the name of the company and the authority under which the company is constituted`
      AND `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the address of the registered office of the company in Singapore or, where it is issued by a branch office, the address of that branch office`
      AND `the certificate states, as at the date of its issue, the class of the shares, whether they are fully or partly paid up and the amount (if any) unpaid on them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every share certificate must be under the common seal ... and must state as at the date of the issue of the certificate" -- a duty: the provision's own question

@ref s 123(2) (src:10512-10528)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 123 act`
`s 123(2) the company must issue share certificates as the subsection requires` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 123(2) issue the share certificate under the seal and stating what the subsection requires`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 123(2) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:10532 | (3) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the rights of
-- src:10533 | any holder of shares.
@ref s 123(3) (src:10532-10533)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with section 123` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(3) the failure affects the rights of a holder of shares` MEANS
    IF `the company has failed to comply with section 123`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section does not affect the rights of any holder of shares"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of a failure to comply with the section

-- src:10535 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:10536 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:10537 | an offence.
@ref s 123(4) (src:10535-10537)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 123` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 123` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j123-1)

-- s 123(4) states no penalty.
@ref s 123(4) (src:10535-10537)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 123` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 123(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (4) creates the offence and states no fine; a general penalty, if any, is in a provision outside these ranges (fork F-j123-2)

§ `Section 124: company may have duplicate common seal`

-- src:10541 | 124. A company may, if authorised by its constitution, have a
-- src:10542 | duplicate common seal which must be a facsimile of the common seal
-- src:10543 | of the company with the addition on its face of the words “Share Seal”
-- src:10544 | and a certificate under such duplicate seal is deemed to be sealed with
-- src:10545 | the common seal of the company for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 124 (src:10541-10545)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company authorises a duplicate common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124 the company may have a duplicate common seal` MEANS
    IF `the constitution of the company authorises a duplicate common seal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may, if authorised by its constitution, have a duplicate common seal" -- a grant whose "if" gate is unmet (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-j124-1)

@ref s 124 (src:10541-10545)
GIVEN `the duplicate seal is a facsimile of the common seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duplicate seal has on its face the addition of the words "Share Seal"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124 the duplicate common seal is as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the duplicate seal is a facsimile of the common seal of the company` AND `the duplicate seal has on its face the addition of the words "Share Seal"`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a duplicate common seal which must be a facsimile of the common seal of the company with the addition on its face of the words “Share Seal”"

@ref s 124 (src:10541-10545)
GIVEN `the certificate is sealed with a duplicate common seal that is as section 124 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124 the certificate is deemed to be sealed with the common seal for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is sealed with a duplicate common seal that is as section 124 requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate under such duplicate seal is deemed to be sealed with the common seal"

§ `Section 125: loss or destruction of certificates`

DECLARE `s 125 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 125(1) issue a duplicate certificate or document in lieu of the one lost or destroyed`

-- s 125(5): subsection (2) does not apply to documents of title to listed securities deposited with the Depository and registered in its name or its nominee's name.
-- src:10598 | (5) Subsection (2) does not apply to documents evidencing title in
-- src:10599 | relation to listed securities which have been deposited with the
-- src:10600 | Depository and registered in its name or its nominee’s name.
@ref s 125(5) (src:10598-10600)
GIVEN `the document evidences title in relation to listed securities which have been deposited with the Depository and registered in its name or its nominee's name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(5) subsection (2) applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document evidences title in relation to listed securities which have been deposited with the Depository and registered in its name or its nominee's name`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply to documents evidencing title in relation to listed securities which have been deposited with the Depository"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of another document

-- s 125(2): where the value is greater than $500 the directors may, before accepting an application, require an advertisement or a bond, or both.
-- A function named for a power, gated by "where": answered as the periods ruling (b) gives it (JUST FALSE) and listed for a lawyer (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3; fork F-j125-1, split site (ii)).
-- src:10565 | (2) Where the value of the shares or debentures represented by the
-- src:10566 | certificate or document is greater than $500 the directors of the
-- src:10567 | company may, before accepting an application for the issue of a
-- src:10568 | duplicate certificate or document, require the applicant —
-- src:10573 | (a) to cause an advertisement to be inserted in a newspaper
-- src:10574 | circulating in a place specified by the directors stating that
-- src:10575 | the certificate or document has been lost or destroyed and
-- src:10576 | that the owner intends after the expiration of 14 days after
-- src:10577 | the publication of the advertisement to apply to the
-- src:10578 | company for a duplicate; or
-- src:10580 | (b) to furnish a bond for an amount equal to at least the current
-- src:10581 | market value of the shares or debentures indemnifying the
-- src:10582 | company against loss following on the production of the
-- src:10583 | original certificate or document,
-- src:10585 | or may require the applicant to do both of those things.
@ref s 125(2) (src:10565-10585)
GIVEN `the value of the shares or debentures represented by the certificate or document, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `subsection (2) applies to the document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(2) the directors may require the applicant to advertise or to furnish a bond, or both` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) applies to the document` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 125(5) "Subsection (2) does not apply to documents evidencing title in relation to listed securities which have been deposited with the Depository"
    ELSE IF `the value of the shares or debentures represented by the certificate or document, in dollars` GREATER THAN 500
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, by the periods ruling (b)): "Where the value of the shares or debentures represented by the certificate or document is greater than $500 the directors of the company may" -- a "may" gated by "where" (listed for a lawyer)

@ref s 125(2) (src:10565-10585)
GIVEN `the day the advertisement was published` IS A DATE
      `the day the owner applies to the company for a duplicate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(2)(a) the owner applies after the expiration of 14 days after the publication of the advertisement` MEANS
    IF `the day the owner applies to the company for a duplicate` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the advertisement was published` 14 Days)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the owner intends after the expiration of 14 days after the publication of the advertisement to apply to the company for a duplicate" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

@ref s 125(2) (src:10565-10585)
GIVEN `the amount of the bond, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the current market value of the shares or debentures, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(2)(b) the bond is for an amount the paragraph allows the directors to require` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the bond, in dollars` AT LEAST `the current market value of the shares or debentures, in dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a bond for an amount equal to at least the current market value of the shares or debentures"

-- s 125(1): the duty to issue a duplicate on payment of a fee not exceeding $2, on the owner's application with a statutory declaration and an undertaking; subject to subsection (2).
-- src:10551 | 125.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), where a certificate or other
-- src:10552 | document of title to shares or debentures is lost or destroyed, the
-- src:10553 | company must on payment of a fee not exceeding $2 issue a duplicate
-- src:10554 | certificate or document in lieu thereof to the owner on the owner’s
-- src:10555 | application accompanied by —
-- src:10557 | (a) a statutory declaration that the certificate or document has
-- src:10558 | been lost or destroyed, and has not been pledged, sold or
-- src:10559 | otherwise disposed of, and, if lost, that proper searches
-- src:10560 | have been made; and
-- src:10562 | (b) an undertaking in writing that if it is found or received by
-- src:10563 | the owner it will be returned to the company.
@ref s 125(1) (src:10551-10563)
GIVEN `the certificate or other document of title to shares or debentures is lost or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner has applied for a duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by a statutory declaration that the certificate or document has been lost or destroyed and has not been pledged, sold or otherwise disposed of and, if lost, that proper searches have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by an undertaking in writing that if the certificate or document is found or received by the owner it will be returned to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee the company requires, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the directors have required the applicant under subsection (2) to advertise or to furnish a bond, or both, and the applicant has not done what was required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(1) the company must issue a duplicate certificate or document to the owner` MEANS
    IF    `the certificate or other document of title to shares or debentures is lost or destroyed`
      AND `the owner has applied for a duplicate`
      AND `the application is accompanied by a statutory declaration that the certificate or document has been lost or destroyed and has not been pledged, sold or otherwise disposed of and, if lost, that proper searches have been made`
      AND `the application is accompanied by an undertaking in writing that if the certificate or document is found or received by the owner it will be returned to the company`
      AND `the fee the company requires, in dollars` AT MOST 2
      AND (NOT `the directors have required the applicant under subsection (2) to advertise or to furnish a bond, or both, and the applicant has not done what was required`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (2), where a certificate ... is lost or destroyed, the company must on payment of a fee not exceeding $2 issue a duplicate ... on the owner's application accompanied by (a) ...; and (b) ..." -- the duty is limited by its own wording; outside it the text is silent (fork F-j125-2)

@ref s 125(1) (src:10551-10563)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 125 act`
`s 125(1) the company must issue a duplicate certificate or document` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 125(1) issue a duplicate certificate or document in lieu of the one lost or destroyed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 125(1) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 125(1) (src:10551-10563)
`s 125(1) the most the company may require as a fee for the duplicate, in dollars` MEANS 2   -- "a fee not exceeding $2"

-- s 125(3): a duplicate issued on or after 30 January 2006 of a share certificate issued before that date states the amount paid and the amount unpaid in place of the historical nominal value.
-- src:10587 | (3) Any duplicate certificate issued on or after 30 January 2006 in
-- src:10588 | respect of a share certificate issued before that date must state, in
-- src:10589 | place of the historical nominal value of the shares, the amount paid on
-- src:10590 | the shares and the amount (if any) unpaid on the shares.
@ref s 125(3) (src:10587-10590)
GIVEN `the day the duplicate certificate was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the share certificate was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(3) the duplicate must state the amount paid and the amount unpaid in place of the historical nominal value of the shares` MEANS
    IF `the day the duplicate certificate was issued` AT LEAST (Date 30 1 2006) AND `the day the share certificate was issued` LESS THAN (Date 30 1 2006)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any duplicate certificate issued on or after 30 January 2006 in respect of a share certificate issued before that date" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- s 125(4): for a book-entry security, a reference to an owner is a reference to the Depository.
-- src:10592 | (4) For the purposes of this section in relation to a book‑entry
-- src:10593 | security, a reference to an owner therein is to be construed as a
-- src:10594 | reference to the Depository.
@ref s 125(4) (src:10592-10594)
GIVEN `the certificate or document relates to a book-entry security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(4) the owner is the Depository` MEANS
    IF `the certificate or document relates to a book-entry security`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a book‑entry security, a reference to an owner therein is to be construed as a reference to the Depository"
